title: Scheduled Task Named gentlemen Created via schtasks
id: b2abdd0e-4374-4911-86dd-1c422cfc6e3b
status: experimental
description: Detects creation of a scheduled task whose name contains the gentlemen string, the task-naming artefact Unit 42 published for the actor it tracks as Storm-2697 and that extortion crews such as The Gentlemen leave behind for persistence and staged encryption. The same guidance pairs this with unsigned or known-vulnerable driver loads such as ThrottleStop.sys, wevtutil clearing of the Security and System logs, and vssadmin or wmic shadow-copy deletion, so treat a hit as one stage of a broader ransomware chain rather than a standalone finding.
references:
  - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/nvidia-investigating-gentlemen-ransomware-breach-claims/
  - https://cybernews.com/security/nvidia-the-gentlemen-ransomware-attack
  - https://ransomware.live/id/TlZJRElBQHRoZWdlbnRsZW1lbg==
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/19
tags:
  - attack.t1053
  - attack.t1486
  - attack.t1490
  - attack.t1657
logsource:
  product: windows
  category: process_creation
detection:
  selection_img:
    Image|endswith: '\schtasks.exe'
  selection_name:
    CommandLine|contains: 'gentlemen'
  condition: selection_img and selection_name
falsepositives:
  - Software packaging or lab tooling that happens to embed the word gentlemen in a task name, which is unlikely outside themed test environments; confirm the parent process before isolating
level: high
